title: Estimate form for plumbers (free PDF) | Jobchit
description: A free, printable plumbing estimate form. Fixtures, pipe material and size, drain and vent work, water heater, sewer or water main, gas line, walls or slab opened, line items and total, with a line for the customer to sign. No account needed.
heading: Estimate for plumbers
sub: Fixtures, pipe, drains, water heater and gas work on one page, with line items, a total and a line for the customer to sign when they say yes.
tips:
  - List each fixture by make and model, and say who supplies it, you or the customer.
  - For each new or replaced run, write the pipe material (PEX, copper, CPVC, PVC or cast iron), the size and about how many feet.
  - For a water heater, write tank or tankless, gallons, fuel, and any venting, gas line or expansion tank work.
  - Say which walls, floors or slab you will open, and whether patching and finishing are in your price or left to the customer.
  - Note what isn't known until you open things up, like the condition of old pipe or the sewer line, and how you will price it if you find a problem.
  - Write who pulls the permit and books the inspection. Put a date the price is good until, and when the customer agrees, have them sign and date it.
